+# it (tmpfs pages are charged to the container too). The stack's total is the sum of its caps:
+# tests/test_live_stack.py holds it under STACK_CPUS and STACK_MEMORY, and live/conftest.py reads
+# every running container's cgroup back before a test runs. The rest of the budget is the host
+# side: pytest and the docker clients, capped by the run's user scope (README), and the docker
+# daemon's own work, which no client can cap. Agents keep the operator's 3g; their CPU is 0.75.
